  ('melt-bar-&-grilled,-gourmet-grilled-cheese-chain,-files-for-bankruptcy', 'Melt Bar & Grilled, Gourmet Grilled Cheese Chain, Files for Bankruptcy', 'Financial struggles force closure of multiple locations in recent years.', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Financial struggles force closure of multiple locations in recent years."},{"type":"p","text":"Melt Bar & Grilled, the renowned Cleveland-based restaurant chain celebrated for its gourmet grilled cheese sandwiches and vast craft beer selection, has officially filed for Chapter 11 bankruptcy protection. The company attributes this decision to the escalating cost of goods and labor, which have significantly impacted its financial stability."},{"type":"p","text":"From Expansion to Downsizing"},{"type":"p","text":"Established in 2006 by Matt Fish, Melt Bar & Grilled experienced rapid growth, reaching over a dozen locations by 2017. However, the company has since faced economic headwinds, leading to the closure of multiple outlets. Currently, Melt Bar & Grilled operates four restaurants in Ohio, located in Akron, Lakewood, Mentor, and Columbus."},{"type":"p","text":"Financial Challenges and Liabilities"},{"type":"p","text":"According to court documents, the company''s liabilities range from $1 million to $10 million, while its assets are estimated to be between $500,000 and $1 million. The bankruptcy filing reveals that Melt Bar & Grilled owes debts to over 100 creditors."},{"type":"p","text":"Restructuring for a Sustainable Future"},{"type":"p","text":"Melt Bar & Grilled aims to utilize the Chapter 11 bankruptcy process to restructure its operations and achieve long-term financial viability. The company believes that this strategic move will enable it to \"ensure its immediate survival and long-term future success.\""},{"type":"p","text":"Industry-Wide Bankruptcy Trend"},{"type":"p","text":"Melt Bar & Grilled''s bankruptcy filing is not an isolated incident. In recent years, numerous restaurant chains have faced similar challenges, leading to bankruptcy filings. Notable examples include Rubio''s, Red Lobster, Party Fowl, Boxer Ramen, Tijuana Flats, Sticky Fingers, Oberweis Dairy, and Foxtrot/Dom''s Kitchen."},{"type":"p","text":"Factors Contributing to Restaurant Bankruptcies"},{"type":"p","text":"Experts attribute the rise in restaurant bankruptcies to various factors, including:"},{"type":"ul","items":["Rising Inflation: The increasing cost of goods and labor has significantly squeezed profit margins for restaurants.","Supply Chain Disruptions: The COVID-19 pandemic and geopolitical events have caused supply chain disruptions, leading to shortages and price increases for essential ingredients and supplies.","Changing Consumer Preferences: Shifting consumer preferences towards healthier and more diverse dining options have posed challenges for some traditional restaurant concepts."]},{"type":"p","text":"Future Outlook"},{"type":"p","text":"As Melt Bar & Grilled navigates the bankruptcy process, the company''s future remains uncertain. Nation''s Restaurant News has reached out to the company for further comments on its restructuring plans and potential closures. The outcome of this bankruptcy filing will undoubtedly have significant implications for the restaurant industry as a whole."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_2a1b6d21afa24eff9f9abbb2dc6388f9~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/June%2019%20Industry%20News.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-19', 'published'),
  ('industry-mourns-the-loss-of-culinary-visionary-james-kent', 'Industry Mourns the Loss of Culinary Visionary James Kent', 'A Tribute to Chef James Kent: Visionary, Innovator, Mentor', '[{"type":"h2","text":"A Tribute to Chef James Kent: Visionary, Innovator, Mentor"},{"type":"p","text":"The restaurant fraternity is in deep mourning following the untimely passing of famous and hardworking, innovative, influential chef James Kent, who shaped the concept of fine dining on 15th June 2024. It is on the backdrop of this sad news that sent shockwaves in the community that many are recalling his great contributions and the irreparable void his absence will leave."},{"type":"p","text":"A Life Dedicated to Excellence in Culinary Arts"},{"type":"p","text":"James Kent, the co-owner and executive chef of Crown Shy and Saga in New York City, has been synonymous with good food and spontaneity for quite a while. Native New Yorker brought up in the city, it didn''t take him very long before getting interested in food. He pursued his dreams vigorously, enrolling at the Prestigious Culinary Institute of America, where he began coming into his own as amazingly talented food-wise. Kent''s rise in the profession was not something less than extraordinary, a former employee of Jean-Georges and Eleven Madison Park, those highly celebrated establishments in which, in early days of work in the profession, he polished his craft and learned esteem for his unique culinary voice."},{"type":"p","text":"Crown Shy and Saga: Hallmarks of Innovation"},{"type":"p","text":"It wasn''t until 2019, with the opening of Crown Shy, that his vision began to take form. The new venture was soon critically acclaimed for its many creative dishes and great dining experience. Nestled in the Financial District, Crown Shy became a vantage point for modern American cuisine, what Kent calls marrying simplicity with sophistication. Crown Shy has established itself as a hot destination not just for everyday diners but for food lovers, too, within a respectably short period."},{"type":"p","text":"After Crown Shy''s success, in 2022 Kent opened Saga with his business partner, Jeff Katz. Located in a historic Art Deco building, Saga proved to be the real clincher on Kent''s résumé as a culinary provocateur. Tasting menus at the restaurant paid homage to Kent''s travels around the world and the diverse food scene of New York. All of these places have huge critical acclaim, with accolades from the Michelin Guide, and are now deeply entrenched as a part of New York dining."},{"type":"p","text":"Remembering a Culinary Giant"},{"type":"p","text":"Kent''s sudden death at 45 has been profound both personally and professionally for all the people who knew him. Many colleagues and friends, and several patrons, went online or used other means to express condolence messages and share their memories of the chef. \"James was not just a chef; he was a mentor, a friend, and a visionary. He will be incredibly missed,\" Katz said in a moving statement. Indeed, many have used this very comment, which speaks to Kent''s generosity, warmth, and inspiration to so many young chefs."},{"type":"p","text":"Celebrity chefs and culinary luminaries have joined in the tribute. \"James had a very special gift for making each person he encountered feel embraced and motivated. His love for cooking was contagious, and the ease with which his imagination flowed was incomparable,\" praised Daniel Humm of Eleven Madison Park."},{"type":"p","text":"The Industry Reflects and Presses On"},{"type":"p","text":"The tragic loss of Kent sends shockwaves throughout the restaurant world, renewing calls for mental health and support for it. The pressure-cooker environment of the culinary world, endless hours at work, constant scrutiny, starts to chip away, even at the toughest of emotions. Industry leaders call for more resources and support systems."},{"type":"p","text":"This is accompanied and balanced by the sudden surge of interest in doing even more in his memory: continuing to push the boundaries of culinary innovation and excellence. Of course, his restaurants Crown Shy and Saga naturally continue his vision and serve as living tributes to his extraordinary talent and dedication."},{"type":"p","text":"A Lasting Legacy"},{"type":"p","text":"The legacy of James Kent lives outside the realm of his restaurants; it is within young chefs whom he trained and in gastronomical dishes that are part of New York''s culinary tapestry. His way of cooking, where he blends tradition with modernity and simplicity with elegance, has forever left its mark on this industry."},{"type":"p","text":"The culinary community''s outpouring with that sense of grief and gratitude speaks to how strong of an impact he had on those around him. The contributions he made will remain part of the foundational makeup of the continuing story called American cuisine as the restaurant world progresses."},{"type":"p","text":"The restaurant community gathers in celebration of James Kent''s life and all he has done, though it is amidst the sorrow and sense of loss that will never be the same again. His accomplishments, his love for food, his progressive nature, and his tenacious strive to personify the craft that he embodied shall never be forgotten and will always be a torch raised high for others who follow in his competitive culinary world. His passing is our collective loss, yet his legacy lives on in the further pursuit of the ideals of excellence and boundless imagination that he championed throughout these rich and storied years."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_43802270779e4b64913d712b9b8d5872~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/New%20blog.jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-18', 'published'),
  ('how-restaurants-are-financially-supporting-pride-month-initiatives?', 'How Restaurants Are Financially Supporting Pride Month Initiatives?', 'Restaurants Raising a Toast (and Funds) to the LGBTQ+ Community', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Restaurants Raising a Toast (and Funds) to the LGBTQ+ Community"},{"type":"p","text":"Pride month in June has become a big marketing opportunity for several brands and businesses including the restaurant industry. Gone are the days when rainbow logos were put on the menu or rainbow cupcakes were sold in limited quantities. Nowadays, restaurants are showing commitments to the LGBTQIA+ community beyond the vibrant aesthetics by supporting the displays of Pride month with real actions."},{"type":"p","text":"From Rainbow Washing to Purposeful Partnerships"},{"type":"p","text":"Earlier, many restaurants faced the backlash for “rainbow washing”. It is a term used to describe businesses that gain benefits from the Pride month symbols without providing enough support to the LGBTQIA+ community. But this year there is a change and we get to see more heartfelt gestures."},{"type":"p","text":"Following are a few examples of how the restaurants are using Pride Month marketing strategically."},{"type":"p","text":"Charity and Donation Partnerships"},{"type":"p","text":"Plenty of restaurants are collaborating with charities and LGBTQIA+ organizations. For instance: Chipotle Mexican Grill is sponsoring up to $25,000 towards GLAAD by selling their rainbow-themed merchandise, “The Pride Edit”. Customers at the register can also round up the amount of their orders with the proceeds going to GLAAD. Using this strategy, customers can have their favorite food and the amount they pay will be sent directly to a worthy cause."},{"type":"p","text":"Employee Empowerment and Inclusivity"},{"type":"p","text":"For LGBTQIA+ community restaurants are making changes by turning their work environment inclusive and friendly. Along with taking part in the Pride Parades, Mexican Chipotle is giving away five hundred “Love What Makes You Real” shirts to their staff members. All these acts show their dedication to fostering an atmosphere at work where diversity is respected."},{"type":"p","text":"Targeted Menu and Menu Promotions"},{"type":"p","text":"Although we may see limited-edition menu items, now they will serve a more significant function. For example, some restaurants might have a menu item curated especially for Pride Month with a donation to the charity for LGBTQIA+ charity."},{"type":"p","text":"The Gen Z Influence and The Rise of Consumer Activism"},{"type":"p","text":"There are plenty of reasons why the marketing for Pride Month has changed and become something more intentional. Firstly, people are becoming more conscious of the growing practice of “rainbow washing” and hold brands responsible for their actions. A big part of this is social media as it has the power to magnify voices and initiate conversations. Gen Z has also become a significant force in the movement. They are the generation known for their support of LGBTQIA+ rights and social activism. Due to this demographic influence, restaurants are adjusting their strategies for marketing."},{"type":"p","text":"Beyond the Rainbow: Addressing Long-Term Issues"},{"type":"p","text":"Although it is a good start to see purposeful marketing strategies during the Pride month, it is critical to recognize that genuine inclusivity extends beyond these short-term campaigns. Earlier there have been problems with the inclusion of LGBTQIA+ and representation in the workforce of restaurants. Restaurants can choose to aim for long-term growth in the following areas:"},{"type":"p","text":"Accessible Restrooms"},{"type":"p","text":"An important step towards the direction of inclusivity would be providing gender-neutral restrooms. This change will show their dedication to meet the needs of every customer, regardless of their gender identity."},{"type":"p","text":"Workplace Diversity and Training"},{"type":"p","text":"It is a constant work for restaurants and other businesses to create an environment at work that is entirely inclusive. These businesses should ensure a welcoming environment for their employees, despite their gender identity or sexual orientation, by inclusive training and investing in the diversity of their staff."},{"type":"p","text":"The Future of Restaurant Marketing During Pride Month"},{"type":"p","text":"It is a good idea for restaurants to provide emphasis on purpose-driven marketing in the Pride Month. It shows a change away from the grand gestures and makes the dining experience more inclusive for each person. Restaurants that give priority to employee empowerment, meaningful partnerships, and inclusivity for the long term are the ones that truly resonate with the customers and foster loyalty. This is because customers demand authenticity and social responsibility from brands. Following are a few trends for the future."},{"type":"p","text":"Hyper-Personalization"},{"type":"p","text":"With Pride Month offerings and promotions, restaurants should use customer insights and data to target particular customer segments of the LGBTQIA+ community."},{"type":"p","text":"Cause-Related Marketing Partnerships"},{"type":"p","text":"Having long-term collaborations between LGBTQIA+ and eateries may result in co-branded menu items, projects, and activities that have a significant impact."},{"type":"p","text":"Restaurants can turn marketing in Pride Month from a passing pad into a meaningful way to show support to the LGBTQIA+ community by placing a high value on inclusivity and embracing purpose. Thus, it will strengthen the bonds with customers, boost customer loyalty, and eventually propel long-term success."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_22036d151b3e4d12aa8ec55a057f857c~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/89-(14-june-news-blog-image2).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-17', 'published'),
  ('the-oscars-of-the-food-world:-2024-james-beard-awards', 'The Oscars of the Food World: 2024 James Beard Awards', 'The Oscars of the Food World: 2024 James Beard Awards Highlight AI in Restaurants', '[{"type":"h2","text":"The Oscars of the Food World: 2024 James Beard Awards Highlight AI in Restaurants"},{"type":"p","text":"The 2024 James Beard Foundation Awards, often referred to as the \"Oscars of the food world,\" celebrated culinary brilliance while shining a spotlight on diverse American regions and cultures that are sometimes overlooked."},{"type":"p","text":"Celebrating Culinary Diversity"},{"type":"p","text":"Chef Serigne Mbaye''s Dakar NOLA, the winner of Best New Restaurant, garnered attention for its modern Senegalese tasting menu, which artfully blends ingredients from New Orleans with Mbaye''s West African heritage. The awards ceremony, held at the Lyric Opera of Chicago, provided a platform for Mbaye to express his pride in showcasing West African cuisine."},{"type":"p","text":"The James Beard Foundation Awards highlighted culinary talent from various backgrounds and regions, featuring winners who presented cuisines from the Philippines, Mexico, Japan, Peru, Vietnam, and Senegal, among others. This year''s awards recognized establishments in smaller cities and states that had not previously received James Beard Awards, signifying a broader recognition of culinary excellence across the country."},{"type":"p","text":"Honoring Smaller Towns and States"},{"type":"p","text":"Chef Paul Smith of 1010 Bridge in Charleston, West Virginia, made history as the first winner from West Virginia, receiving the Best Chef: Southeast award. Lula Drake Wine Parlour in Columbia, South Carolina, was honored with the Best Wine and Other Beverage Program award. The awards also acknowledged chefs from Easton, Maryland; Mystic, Connecticut; and Mission, Texas, further emphasizing the diversity of culinary talent across the United States."},{"type":"p","text":"New Culinary Careers"},{"type":"p","text":"The James Beard Awards celebrated chefs who found their culinary calling through unique journeys. Masako Morishita, originally from Japan, transitioned from cheering for the Washington Commanders to winning the Emerging Chef Award for her Japanese comfort food at Perry''s in Washington, DC. Atsuko Fujimoto, who moved to Portland, Maine, 23 years ago without any prior professional kitchen experience, was honored with the Outstanding Baker award."},{"type":"p","text":"Addressing Industry Challenges"},{"type":"p","text":"The event addressed critical issues facing the restaurant industry, including mental health, inclusivity, climate change, and sustainability. Ruth Reichl, a renowned food writer who received a Lifetime Achievement Award, acknowledged the James Beard Foundation''s role in transforming American cuisine. She had coined the phrase \"Oscars of the food world\" over three decades ago in her reporting on the inaugural awards."},{"type":"p","text":"The James Beard Foundation, a non-profit organization founded in 1986, has implemented new rules and guidelines to address past criticisms regarding lack of diversity and misconduct by chefs. Winners expressed optimism that positive changes in culinary culture will continue, with Best Chef: Northwest & Pacific winner Gregory Gourdet emphasizing the importance of female-led teams, diversity, and inclusivity."},{"type":"p","text":"Restaurant and Chef Award Winners"},{"type":"ul","items":["Outstanding Chef: Michael Rafidi, Albi, Washington, D.C.","Outstanding Restaurant: Kann, Portland, Oregon","Best New Restaurant: The Restaurant at Justin, Justin, Texas","Emerging Chef: Rene Redzepi, Noma, Copenhagen, Denmark & Brooklyn, New York","Outstanding Bar: Julep, Houston","Outstanding Pastry Chef or Baker: Margarita Manzke, République, Los Angeles","Outstanding Hospitality: Sepia, Chicago"]},{"type":"p","text":"Best Chefs by Region"},{"type":"ul","items":["California: Brandon Jew, Mister Jiu''s, San Francisco","Great Lakes: Andrew Zimmerman and Mike Delay, Sepia, Chicago","Mid-Atlantic: Peter Chang, Peter Chang, multiple locations","Midwest: Yia Vang, Union Hmong Kitchen, Minneapolis","Mountain: Caroline Glover, Annette, Aurora, Colorado","New York State: Chintan Pandya, Dhamaka, New York City","Northeast (excluding New York State): Valentine Howell, The Beehive, Bristol, Rhode Island","Northwest & Pacific: Crystal Wahpepah, Wahpepah''s Kitchen, Oakland, California","South: Terry Koval, The Deer and the Dove, Decatur, Georgia","Southeast: Mashama Bailey, The Grey, Savannah, Georgia","Southwest: Fernando Olea, Sazón, Santa Fe, New Mexico","Texas: Iliana de la Vega, El Naranjo, Austin"]},{"type":"p","text":"Note: The list of winners above is not exhaustive. For a complete list of winners and nominees, please refer to the official James Beard Foundation website."},{"type":"p","text":"The 2024 James Beard Foundation Awards showcased a vibrant and evolving culinary landscape in the United States, celebrating diversity, regional flavors, and the dedication of chefs and restaurateurs to their craft. The awards also acknowledged the challenges faced by the industry while emphasizing the importance of inclusivity and sustainability."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_4f0bfce3a02342aba02b85b8127e6940~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/93(17june-News-blog).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-16', 'published'),
  ('franchise-fever:-2024-expo-ignites-entrepreneurial-spirit-with-thousands-of-attendees', 'Franchise Fever: 2024 Expo Ignites Entrepreneurial Spirit with Thousands of Attendees', 'Thousands Flock to 2024 Franchise Expo, Fueling Business Ambitions', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Thousands Flock to 2024 Franchise Expo, Fueling Business Ambitions"},{"type":"p","text":"The 2024 International Franchise Expo (IFE) enjoyed gorgeous weather in New York City last week, welcoming thousands of attendees to the iconic Javits Center. Over 300 franchise exhibitors showcased a diverse range of industries, from automotive and beauty to technology and food. Attendees were eager to discover new brands, network with industry professionals, and learn from educational sessions."},{"type":"p","text":"Innovative Concepts Take Center Stage"},{"type":"p","text":"On the show floor, the On the Hook food truck concept stood out. President Ocean Andrew, son of an Alaskan fisherman, emphasized the brand''s focus on family-friendly work hours and community-based operations. Colette Bell, founder of Ace Handyman, highlighted the importance of customer service in driving their success as the top handyman franchise in the country."},{"type":"p","text":"Franchise Vendors and Suppliers Offer Key Support"},{"type":"p","text":"The expo also featured numerous vendors and suppliers crucial to franchise success. Sebastian Aguirre of NiceJob shared how his company has helped hundreds of franchises with online reputation management. The franchise law firm Spadea Lignana showcased their cloud-based system for simplifying Franchise Disclosure Document updates."},{"type":"p","text":"Educational Sessions Empower Aspiring Franchisees"},{"type":"p","text":"IFE 2024 offered over 70 workshops and sessions. The \"Women in Franchising: Being Successful in Today’s Marketplace\" panel featured accomplished women sharing insights on teamwork, mentorship, and the importance of diversity in business. Steve Beagelman of SMB Franchise Advisors presented \"Should You Franchise Your Business?\", guiding potential franchisors through key considerations like control, communication, and capital requirements."},{"type":"p","text":"Culinary Delights and Industry Trends"},{"type":"p","text":"Attendees enjoyed a plethora of food samples, with chicken being a dominant theme among exhibitors. Beyond specific franchises, the expo highlighted trends like sustainability, technology integration in services, and the growing wellness industry."},{"type":"p","text":"Networking and Collaboration Opportunities Abound"},{"type":"p","text":"IFE served as a vital hub for networking and collaboration. Attendees connected with fellow entrepreneurs, industry experts, and franchisors, fostering potential partnerships and investments."},{"type":"p","text":"The Future of Franchising"},{"type":"p","text":"The trends showcased at IFE 2024 point to a bright future for the franchising sector. Businesses are embracing technology to meet evolving consumer demands, with a growing emphasis on sustainability and innovation. The expo''s success underscores the resilience and adaptability of the franchise model, promising continued growth and evolution in the years to come."},{"type":"p","text":"Overall, the 2024 International Franchise Expo provided a comprehensive look at the current landscape and future potential of the franchising industry, leaving attendees inspired and eager for the next edition."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_1407826a91cd45c3951e2e5710ff6148~mv2.jpg/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c,q_90/80-(13june-News-report).jpg', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-15', 'published'),
  ('mcdonald’s-empowers-black-fashion-designers-with-new-initiative', 'McDonald’s Empowers Black Fashion Designers with New Initiative', 'Beyond the Golden Arches: McDonald''s New Program Elevates Black Fashion Talent', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Beyond the Golden Arches: McDonald''s New Program Elevates Black Fashion Talent"},{"type":"p","text":"To encourage and assist Black fashion designers, McDonald''s launches the Black and Positively Golden Change of Fashion initiative. Due to the low percentage of Black designers in the United States (7.3%), the McDonald''s program is extremely important. McDonald''s I addressed the issues of diversity in the industry with this launch. Given that this program is a comprehensive undertaking, its launch has had a significant impact on interest. For a year-long mentorship, this initiative pairs five up-and-coming designers with five seasoned Black industry professionals."},{"type":"p","text":"This handbook contains industry insights, useful suggestions, and the mentors'' individualized coaching. These revelations would impede the designer''s career advancement. The launch of a capsule collection that showcases the undeniable and extraordinary talent of the chosen designers."},{"type":"p","text":"Financial and Mentorship Support:"},{"type":"p","text":"The biggest problem that black designers have is funding, which McDonald''s addresses. The designers don''t have to worry about the money for creating the designs, they can concentrate on creating the designs with no tension as McDonald''s provided a total of $200,000 in financial funding. The master classes that are conducted by experienced designers provide them the insight into the industry guidelines and serve as a helping hand. This knowledge would help the designers in the long run."},{"type":"p","text":"Impact and Importance:"},{"type":"p","text":"The Black and Positively Golden Change of Fashion initiative from McDonald''s encourages diversity and the advancement of Black designers in the fashion sector. The goal of this initiative is to empower black designers to spur change within the industry. McDonald''s is prepared to keep highlighting the accomplishments and potential of Black designers, as it has done well in the past. The well-known mentors would help the designers succeed and provide them with insightful advice. Famous designers Elaine Welteroth and Jacqueline Cooper have been brought in by McDonald''s to coach the designers and provide them with vital industry insights and guidance."},{"type":"p","text":"Broader Campaign Context:"},{"type":"p","text":"The empowerment of the Black community is the main goal of McDonald''s large Black and Positively Golden initiative. McDonald''s has already taken several actions in this regard and is still doing well. It started back in 2019 to offer a successful helping hand. This initiative has helped the black community and brought an empowering change. McDonald''s has ensured to help in various spheres including education and empowerment. The Change of Fashion program, which highlights the brand''s long-term dedication to supporting the Black community, is the campaign''s extension."},{"type":"p","text":"Personal Stories:"},{"type":"p","text":"The show includes personal stories, Larissa Muehleder''s being one of them. Larissa''s story serves as an excellent example of how the program can significantly impact Black designers'' careers. It disproves the designers'' positive experiences and the way it changed their lives."},{"type":"p","text":"Future Implications:"},{"type":"p","text":"The success of McDonald''s Black and Positively Golden Change of Fashion initiative serves as a model for other businesses. It inspires people to support Black creators with comparable endeavors. There has been a long-lasting positive influence from these programs. McDonald''s has demonstrated an extraordinary commitment to social responsibility, and these activities are valued by the company''s devoted consumer base."},{"type":"p","text":"Expanding Opportunities:"},{"type":"p","text":"Opportunities under the McDonald''s Black and Positively Golden Change of Fashion program have increased. This initiative benefits individual designers as well as providing opportunities inside the fashion industry. This curriculum encourages a diversified worldview and questions accepted industry conventions. Through this program, a more positive perspective has been brought to the globe by displaying the brilliance and originality of Black designers."},{"type":"p","text":"Through cooperation and mentoring, aspiring designers could get access to networks and resources that were previously unavailable. They have achieved long-term success as a result. The fashion business now offers more chances and is more representative of a range of views and experiences thanks to this program."},{"type":"p","text":"McDonald’s Black and Positively Golden Change of Fashion program is a commendable move in the direction of expansion and diversity. It has addressed the critical void present in the fashion sector. McDonald''s has given Black designers media visibility, financial backing, and mentoring. This not only advances the careers of these designers but also brings about a shift in the industry as a whole. This initiative is a calculated part of McDonald''s continuous attempts to promote inclusivity and diversity, enhancing the company''s reputation as a socially conscious one."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_0e321335e614411792096823f2c39a1f~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_1920,h_1080,al_c/image%20(14).png', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-14', 'published'),
  ('experience-l.a.''s-unique-pizza-fusion:-cheesy-crusts-and-korean-bbq-toppings', 'Experience L.A.''s Unique Pizza Fusion: Cheesy Crusts and Korean BBQ Toppings', 'Korean BBQ Pizza: L.A.''s Unexpected & Delicious Food Fusion Trend', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Korean BBQ Pizza: L.A.''s Unexpected & Delicious Food Fusion Trend"},{"type":"p","text":"Los Angeles is renowned for its multiculturalism, which extends to the sense of taste. L.A.''s unique pizza culture is renowned for its flavor fusions. There are currently a tonne of alternatives due to the innovation in pizza culture, which started with traditional experiments and moved into modern ones. From the first, innovative smoked salmon pizza to the newest craze of Korean BBQ toppings. The evolution of L.A.''s pizza culture is evidence of the city''s spirit of culinary innovation."},{"type":"p","text":"The unmatched pizza experience of L.A. is all about the classical taste with international spice twists. Let''s take a tour around the colorful and varied world of pizza, emphasizing the places you simply must see and the creative tastes that characterize this thriving culinary scene."},{"type":"p","text":"The Birth of a Pizza Revolution"},{"type":"p","text":"When Wolfgang Puck introduced his smoked salmon pizza at Spago in the early 1980s, it revolutionized the pizza industry. This marked the start of Los Angeles'' transformation as a cosmopolitan center for pizza. His approach opened the door for other cooks to try new things. They brought in new tastes and aesthetics, resulting in a pizza culture that is constantly changing."},{"type":"p","text":"Embracing Diverse Styles"},{"type":"p","text":"The variety-rich L.A. pizza places are a landmark for the pizza lovers. Whether it be the cheesy crusts which are thick and chewy or the crispy foldable pizzas it covers so much and more. Each innovative pizza is better than the other inspired by the Neapolitan style. Every pizza enthusiast can find something to their liking. By incorporating regional ingredients and special techniques, the local chefs further enrich the diversity."},{"type":"p","text":"Fusion of Flavors: Korean BBQ Pizza"},{"type":"p","text":"Right now, combining the flavors of Korean BBQ with conventional pizza has to be one of the most interesting trends. This has given the pizza culture of Los Angeles a delicious touch. This combines the best elements of Korean and traditional flavors. Thus, the creative culture provides a distinctive experience that satisfies our palates."},{"type":"p","text":"Seven Tigers Pie Club"},{"type":"p","text":"We are introduced to the combination of Detroit-style pizza with L.A. and a dash of Korean ideas at this restaurant, which is headed by Alex Sign. This yields an incredibly delicious assortment of pizzas. These have fusion-type toppings that incorporate Korean BBQ ingredients into the classic Los Angeles style."},{"type":"p","text":"Notable Pizzerias Leading the Charge"},{"type":"p","text":"Many pizzerias in Los Angeles have expanded the definition of conventional pizza, resulting in distinctive and remarkable dining experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"One of the well-known is the Leopardo, which is run by chef Joshua Skenes, a renowned and highly acclaimed chef with an adventurous flair. Leopardo is about so much more than just homemade mozzarella. They leave no opportunities to impress with the wild-yeasted dough formed from stone ground floors. This eatery serves pizza created through experimentation and vivid combinations."},{"type":"p","text":"The Fiorelli Pizza, which comes from the Cooks Garden in Venice, is another item on the list. This one places more focus on using locally farmed and fresh ingredients. Their strategy promotes sustainability and guarantees high-quality products. Through its internet platform, it keeps a tight relationship with its clients."},{"type":"p","text":"Essential Pizzas to Try in L.A."},{"type":"p","text":"Pizza culture in Los Angeles is characterized by creativity, variety, and innovation. Let''s talk about some pizzas that highlight the culinary inventiveness of the city:"},{"type":"p","text":"First on the list is folk pizza, which is renowned for its tenacity in fermenting dough. This one has a wide, robust rim that preserves all of the components. To taste something different, try the traditional pepperoni or fennel sausage pizza."},{"type":"p","text":"The Pizzana, a contemporary twist on Neapolitan pizza, comes next. enhanced with discussions of locally grown veggies, other special sauces, and sausages produced in-house."},{"type":"p","text":"A must-try is the Gjelina. It was acclaimed for its wood-fired pizza which is fusions with tradition and modern-day innovation. Using toppings and seasonal, fresh foods."},{"type":"p","text":"These days, pizza enthusiasts flock to Los Angeles. It combines current innovation and diversity with traditional flavor. Whether you want to stick with traditional looks or take a bold step forward with cutting-edge fusions and experiments. Pizza culture in Los Angeles has something for everyone. Taste the fusion to give your taste buds an unparalleled experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_abbf08bfdde7414db2fcb560180ce78a~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_3000,h_2000,al_c/image%20(14).png', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-13', 'published'),
  ('securing-the-plate:-the-restaurant-industry’s-cyber-fraud-battle', 'Securing the Plate: The Restaurant Industry’s Cyber Fraud Battle', 'Digital Dining Dangers: The Rising Threat of Cyberattacks on Restaurants', '[{"type":"h2","text":"Digital Dining Dangers: The Rising Threat of Cyberattacks on Restaurants"},{"type":"p","text":"In a time when technology is king, the fight against cybercrime has reached previously unprecedented heights. As the food industry is adjusting to the modern age, new measures are coming upfront to protect restaurant gift card transactions from online threats. To ensure that your meal is both safe and tasty, restaurants from all over the world are stepping up."},{"type":"p","text":"Embracing Digital Integration in Restaurants"},{"type":"p","text":"Any modern restaurant you visit is probably going to have a lot of digital gadgets that are all seamlessly incorporated into the dining experience. Our interactions with our favorite restaurants have been completely transformed by technology, from contactless payment methods to tablets for ordering. But these technological advances also bring vulnerabilities, so restaurateurs are strengthening their digital fortifications with every measure possible."},{"type":"p","text":"The Increasing Threat of Cyber Fraud"},{"type":"p","text":"\"Cyber Fraud is more common than ever, but there are a multitude of measures that can be implemented to ensure profits and customers don''t suffer,\" says Sivakumar Vinayagam, an expert in cybersecurity and software engineering. He is currently the Lead Systems Architect for Netmasons and its service Securetree, and he has over ten years of experience in the field."},{"type":"p","text":"Expertise in Restaurant Gift Card Security"},{"type":"p","text":"With almost 1,000 clients, Vinayagam is a software specialist in the restaurant gift card market. He works with different restaurant groups and, through his system implementations and programming skills, has saved businesses millions of dollars. \"I want small and medium-sized businesses to feel like they have security, substantial reach, and success even in the absence of substantial resources or time,\" he says."},{"type":"p","text":"Implementing Cutting-Edge Encryption"},{"type":"p","text":"The restaurant industry''s primary line of defense against cyberattacks is encryption. According to Vinayagam, \"Restaurants thwart the attempts of cybercriminals aiming to intercept transactions by encoding sensitive information such as credit card details and customer data.\" To stop fraud, he uses distinct gift card numbers and keeps an eye out for odd activity."},{"type":"p","text":"Ensuring Robust Cybersecurity"},{"type":"p","text":"Vinayagam''s function as a cybersecurity expert depends heavily on these integrated security measures. It is possible to stop fraudsters from taking advantage of gift card systems by putting these safeguards in place, protecting both the consumers and the participating businesses."},{"type":"p","text":"Raising the Bar with PCI Compliance"},{"type":"p","text":"The standard for protecting credit card information is established by the Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard or PCI DSS. Restaurants need to make sure that every part of their digital infrastructure satisfies the highest security standards by carefully following these strict guidelines. To guarantee compliance, Vinayagam places a strong emphasis on access control procedures and frequent network monitoring."},{"type":"p","text":"Heightened Vigilance Against Phishing Scams"},{"type":"p","text":"Phishing scams are still a major problem in the digital world, endangering both consumers and businesses. Restaurants are actively teaching their employees and customers how to spot phishing attempts. Vinayagam states, \"Eateries can stay one step ahead of cybercriminals by fostering a culture of vigilance.\" His proprietary Fraud Score system aids in identifying and examining questionable transactions."},{"type":"p","text":"Deploying Advanced Fraud Detection Systems"},{"type":"p","text":"Restaurants are using sophisticated fraud detection systems as part of the ongoing arms race against cyber fraud. These systems analyze transactional data in real time to spot anomalies and questionable activity using machine learning and artificial intelligence algorithms. \"Eateries are protecting their customers and reputation by detecting fraudulent behavior before it escalates,\" claims Vinayagam."},{"type":"p","text":"Empowering Consumers with Security Awareness"},{"type":"p","text":"In the fight against cyber fraud, education is essential. Vinayagam states, \"Eateries need to educate consumers about the importance of secure transactions and the risks associated with cyber threats, whether through informative signage or digital campaigns.\" He thinks restaurants can increase customer loyalty and trust by cultivating a security-conscious culture."},{"type":"p","text":"Building Trust Through Security Consciousness"},{"type":"p","text":"According to Vinayagam, \"In an era where technology permeates every aspect of our lives, the fight against cyber fraud is more critical than ever.\" \"In my quest to protect against cyber threats, I worked hard to look into every possibility. I want both restaurant owners and patrons to feel secure and at ease.”"},{"type":"p","text":"Cybersecurity becomes essential as the restaurants embrace technology. PCI compliance, encryption, and fraud detection systems protect the gift card information. Educating diners and staff on cyber scams keeps everyone safe. By giving priority to security, restaurants can ensure a secure and delightful dining experience."},{"type":"p","text":"Disclaimer: This article is informative and not for promotional purposes. Moreover, the content belongs to the owner and there are no affiliations or marketing motives behind it."},{"type":"p","text":"For media inquiries, please contact:"},{"type":"p","text":"PR Team | pr@eatOS.com | +1 424 401 0184"},{"type":"p","text":"About eatOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Since 2017, eatOS has championed \"Restaurants Made Simple\" through its integrated ecosystem of products. This AI-driven restaurant management technology, tailored for boutique eateries and large-scale chains, boasts an advanced Point of Sale, intuitive kitchen interfaces, table-side ordering and payment solutions, self-service kiosks, and an expansive online ordering and delivery platform. We''re redefining the dining landscape, ensuring efficiency, and elevating guest experiences."},{"type":"p","text":"eatOS POS Inc. | 1111 Brickell Avenue FL 10, Miami, FL 33131 | eatOS.com"}]', 'https://static.wixstatic.com/media/0d9b20_f93c8d3dbb014f198ae95078d6af1ce0~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_4000,h_3000,al_c/cyber.png', 'Industry News', 'eatOS Staff', '2024-06-12', 'published');
